title: Authorizations › Case page › Risk analysis › Pop-ups
route: /authorizations/case/R-1042?tab=risk
intro: The two dialogs on the Risk analysis tab: the full list of comparable decisions, and the plain-words explanation of how the approval chance is calculated.
dir: TD
---
group gA "See all"
  click sa "Click 'See all' on 'Comparable decisions'"
  overlay m1 "Dialog 'Comparable decisions'\n'6 of the closest matches from your own and the network's history'"
  process rw "Six rows, each with who, match and an outcome pill\nThe three from the card, then three more"
  process mr "The extra rows\n'Same payer, plan named, scores falling' (Network, close match)\n'Earlier attempt not documented' (Yours, close match)\n'Recent relapse, no step-down named' (Network, partial match)"
  process dy "Outcomes use the request's own days\ne.g. 'Approved 14/14' or 'Approved 7/14' for a 14-day request"
  click c1 "Click 'Close'"
endgroup

group gB "How it is calculated"
  click hc "Click 'How it is calculated'"
  overlay m2 "Dialog 'How the approval chance is calculated'\n'In plain words. Updated nightly.'"
  agent s1 "1 Historian finds similar decisions\nSame payer and plan, level of care, diagnosis cluster, review type and documentation signals"
  agent s2 "2 Forecaster starts from the base rate\nHow often the payer approved those requests as asked"
  process s3 "3 It adds and takes away points\nEach row is something the draft shows, or does not show yet"
  process s4 "4 The range says how sure it is\nWith little history it says 'Benchmark estimate'"
  agent s5 "5 It is checked every night\nForecaster compares what it said with what payers decided"
  process nt "Footer: 'It estimates how well the paperwork fits the payer's past decisions. It does not decide care, never blocks a request, and is never shown to payers or patients.'"
  click c2 "Click 'Got it'"
endgroup

click cx "Click the X, click the dimmed area, or press Esc"
end e "Dialog closes\nYou are back on Risk analysis, nothing changed"

sa --> m1 --> rw --> mr --> dy --> c1 --> e
m1 --> cx
hc --> m2 --> s1 --> s2 --> s3 --> s4 --> s5 --> nt --> c2 --> e
m2 --> cx
cx --> e
